       "type": "text",
       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses can also cause shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nIf the dose was a typo, I can enter one of these instead:\n- **5 mg orally once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg orally once daily.** This is the maximum labeled dose.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or tell me if you meant a different drug or strength. If you need more than 10 mg/day of antihypertensive effect, adding a second agent from another class is the standard approach. I can enter that order too."
      }
