       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and the dose is 5 times the labeled maximum of 10 mg/day. Confirming it doesn't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg orally once daily.** This is the labeled maximum. I can add a note on the order that the patient is on a high-dose protocol under pharmacist review.\n- **Enter 5 mg orally once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **Add a second antihypertensive from another class.** This is the standard way to get more effect than 10 mg of amlodipine gives.\n\nIf a protocol really does call for a dose above the label, the prescriber can enter it directly through the hospital's own override process. That process includes pharmacy verification and a hard-stop review. Tell me if you'd like me to enter one of the options above."
      }
